Hello group, I was looking through the gallery <http://shiny.rstudio.com/gallery/> and cannot find a good template for trying to model something rather simple. What I want to do is take some users in two generic groups (1 and 2), list them down the side of a graph with two x-axes (group 1 on X1, group 2 on X2) with no y-axis, and then draw a line between a member of group 1 and group 2 when the user indicates they are connected.

output could look like this, but graphical.
Group 1 Group 2
A            9
B            6
C            7
D            5
E           11
F            2
G           4

For example, if the user indicated that there was an association between C and 4, imagine a line is drawn between Group 1 (C) and Group 2 (4). I know how I would model the data inputting* but don't know how to draw the graphical representation. I wanted it to update in real time so I chose Shiny but maybe python is better for this (or I may need to dust off my java.awt.* ... oh noes!! ....)

thx!
Chris

