Hi Stepan,
We can't provide any legal advice ourselves, but given that you aren't bundling shiny server with an offering that you are distributing you likely don't need to worry about shiny server being licensed under an AGPL license so you could run your own shiny server in the cloud (AWS, Azure, Google etc...) and/or you can also use shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> to host your running shiny applications if you so desire.     With shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>, we would be operating the service for you and you can focus on the creation of your applications.  As long as you aren't using our trademark (and it sounds like you aren't hosting the IDE), you should be good to go.  Again, we aren't lawyers and can't dispense legal advice, but hopefully that gives you a sense for what is possible.
Best,
-Tareef

